"Add working members (one new unique role each) to a team created in this session, by exact team ID or unique name. Every team gets a coordinator and a monitor from Sova, which this team already has: name only the workers. Each team runs 2 more workers than you name, so small independent jobs are cheaper as separate workers (agent_spawn). New members see the current roster in their header, and the coordinator is told about each one with its assignment. Teams restored from history are read-only. Same validation and rollback as agent_spawn; the team's create-time defaults apply. Name a work kind for every member (kind: planning, investigation, routine or complex): it runs on that kind's model from this chat's subagent profile (or its fallback); a member with neither a kind nor a model is refused unless the profile is Off. Limits: no per-request limit. A team seats 24 members, the coordinator and monitor Sova adds included. This chat runs at most 24 workers at once, idle ones and every team member (coordinator and monitor included) counted; a request that would pass either is refused before anything starts, and Sova never stops a worker to make room. members must be a list of member objects (one role each). A member takes role, prompt, ownedPaths, backend, model, effort, tools, mcpServers, systemPrompt, cwd, wake, backendOptions, extensions, kind (extensions e.g. [\"npm:pi-web-access\"]); count, fork, agentType and any other setting are refused (one member per role; agent_spawn for fork or agentType). Only the coordinator hands a member over to a successor (its team_succeed); once no coordinator is live, the main chat can start a replacement with team_succeed."
